REST API is a standard way for two systems
 to talk to each other over the internet using HTTP.

Think of it like shopping online 🛒
👉🏻 You browse products → place order → get delivery.
👉🏻 Same way: App sends a request → server processes it → app gets data.

REST = Representational State Transfer

✅ R – Representational
You don’t send raw data — you send representations like JSON or XML.

✅ S – State
Server doesn’t remember you.
Every request carries everything it needs → stateless.

✅ T – Transfer
Data is transferred using HTTP methods:
GET (read) • POST (create) • PUT (update) • DELETE (remove)

👉🏻 Real-life example (Bank App):
• Check account balance → GET
• Transfer money → POST
• Update profile details → PUT
• Close account → DELETE